      "text": "in P3 it selects approximately 1.40 days and its 0.70-day harmonic as separate signals. SkillEvolver succeeds on P1 and P3, while CoEvoSkills fails both. On the replacement- data P2 instance, both skills receive zero, giving the case a specific transfer pattern across the three changes. Scheduling locates the difference at a constraint that de- termines correctness. SkillEvolver’s artifact explicitly pre- serves baseline-relative right shifts and precedence-aware local minimality. The executor carries these rules across re- named inputs, a replacement scheduling instance, and an added machine-handoff requirement, passing all three vari- ants; SPARK also passes all three. CoEvoSkills passes P3, but its P1 output fails the local-minimality check: an opera- tion starts at 29 with an anchor of 24 and can move earlier. The other structural and policy checks pass. This trace-based attribution connects the outcome to preservation of a repair invariant. Together, the cases illustrate a transferable skill as a set of diagnostic and constraint-preserving decisions that the executor adapts to the new task.",
